//! smp — the application processors: started, each with its own state,
//! and parked idle while the boot processor runs every thread (px161, SMP
//! stage 1; px138's plan, its stage 1 row).
//!
//! **Bring-up, in two steps.** Limine's MP feature (boot/start.S's
//! request, flags 0) started every processor its MP response lists and
//! parked each in its own loop, which polls the processor's `goto_address`
//! (bootloader-reclaimable memory, never handed out by kernel/frames) and
//! spins: with 16 processors on 8 host threads under KVM, a boot that left
//! them there until kernel/user's start took 820 ms where one with none
//! started took 480 ms, most of it before kernel/apic's start. So `hold`,
//! the kernel's first step, sends each to boot/isr.S's `pax_ap_hold`: CLI;
//! HLT on Limine's tables and stack, an IDT of its own with only the NMI's
//! gate, until its record appears in its hold words. Under `nosmp`, and
//! past MAX, a processor goes to `pax_ap_park` (CLI; HLT) instead.
//!
//! `start_aps` (kmain_console, after kernel/user's `start`: the boot
//! processor's CR0, CR4, EFER and SYSCALL MSRs are final then, and
//! kernel/timer has its calibration) numbers the response's entries other
//! than the boot processor's 1, 2, … in its order: index i. For each, up to
//! MAX in all, a window of 256 KiB at CPUS + i × SPAN (PML4 slot 417, its
//! tables made now, before the first process copies the kernel half)
//! holds, each page from kernel/frames, read-write, no-execute:
//!
//!     +0x00000  the record (kernel/percpu: 512 bytes, its GDT and TSS in it)
//!     +0x08000  the idle stack, 16 KiB      (+0x01000 to +0x08000 a guard)
//!     +0x10000  IST1, the double fault's     +0x18000 IST2, the NMI's
//!     +0x20000  IST3, the machine check's    +0x28000 IST4, #DB's
//!
//! each stack 16 KiB above 16 KiB never mapped: 21 frames, 84 KiB, a
//! processor. The boot processor writes the record (its index, APIC ID,
//! ACPI UID, idle stack top, CURRENT the idle mark), the GDT and TSS
//! (kernel/gdt's `fill_ap`: RSP0 the idle stack, IST1-4 its own four) and
//! publishes in boot/isr.S's `pax_ap_boot`, before any release:
//!
//!     0 W_CR3 the kernel's PML4   1 W_MAIN pax_ap_main's address
//!     2 W_CR0, 3 W_CR4, 4 W_EFER, 5 W_XCR0 (when CR4.OSXSAVE),
//!     6 W_STAR, 7 W_LSTAR, 8 W_FMASK: the boot processor's own
//!     10 W_STOPPED, 11 W_REPORTED: the stopped processors, by bit
//!
//! Then each is released: its record stored into its second hold word with
//! release semantics, every record first, and then one NMI to each once its
//! first word says HELD (its gate is loaded then, and it looks at the
//! record only on that gate's return: the NMI is taken in the hold, never
//! after the processor went on, where no gate of PAX's is ready for it). It
//! writes the record into `extra_argument` and goes on to `pax_ap_entry`,
//! as if Limine had sent it there. The boot processor waits up to a second
//! by kernel/clock for each to say HELD and then IDLE, and names any that
//! never did. A processor PAX does not run (`nosmp`
//! on the command line, one past MAX, one whose window memory refused, one
//! that never reached its idle loop) gets INIT (`park`): it waits for a startup IPI
//! as it did before any bootloader started it, which is what the
//! one-processor fallback, `nosmp`, gives back.
//!
//! **An application processor** enters at `pax_ap_entry` (PAX's tables,
//! its own stack, GDT, TSS, the one IDT, GS its record), then
//! `pax_ap_main`: IA32_GS_BASE read back into its record (GS_SEEN), CR0,
//! CR4, XCR0, EFER, STAR, LSTAR and FMASK set to the boot processor's, its
//! local APIC as the boot processor's (kernel/apic's `ap_start`: x2APIC when
//! that one is, spurious vector 47, its APIC ID held to Limine's), its tick
//! armed with the boot processor's calibration (kernel/timer's `ap_arm`:
//! 100 Hz on vector 32), STATE IDLE, then for ever: WAKES + 1; STI; HLT;
//! CLI (boot/isr.S's `pax_ap_halt`). It runs no thread: its CURRENT is
//! the idle mark, and kernel/sched's tick and switch stop a processor
//! other than CPU 0 by name (kernel/percpu's `boot_only`).
//!
//! **Its interrupts** (kernel/interrupts sends every vector it takes but
//! the NMI here, `ap_interrupt`): vector 32, its tick, is counted (TICKS)
//! and acknowledged at its local APIC; 47, its local APIC's spurious
//! interrupt, counted and not acknowledged (SDM vol. 3A §11.9); anything
//! else stops it, the vector, error, RIP and CR2 in its record. Its NMI
//! (`ap_nmi`, on its own IST2) is counted, the frame's address kept, and
//! it resumes. The 8259's line reaches CPU 0 alone (LINT0, kernel/apic),
//! MSI names CPU 0's APIC ID, and every other LVT entry Limine masked: an
//! application processor takes its tick, NMIs and its spurious vector.
//!
//! **What is said.** With one processor, nothing (no line of any boot
//! changes). With more: `cpus: application processors idle K of M in T
//! ms, 84 KiB each (N KiB with their tables); the boot processor runs every
//! thread`, a line for each
//! that never reached its idle loop, then the private-state check
//! (`check`): every processor's record, GDT and TSS its own, each TSS's
//! RSP0 and IST1-4 inside its own window (CPU 0's: boot/isr.S's IST
//! stacks), GS's base as each processor read it its own record:
//! `cpus: private state checked: N processors, no record, GDT, TSS or
//! stack shared`, or what was shared, by name. `pax.cpunmi` (a test's
//! word) then sends each idle processor one NMI and says whether each took
//! it on its own IST2. A stopped processor is named by the boot processor
//! at its next tick (`report_stops`): an application processor never
//! writes the log. /proc/pax-cpus reads the rest (kernel/procfs).
//!
//! Written from: the Limine protocol (PROTOCOL.md at 3a0526b7: the MP
//! feature, its response and `struct limine_mp_info`, the release store,
//! the machine state at entry); the Intel SDM vol. 3A §2.5 (CR0, CR4),
//! §2.6 (XCR0), §5.8.8 (STAR, LSTAR, FMASK), §6.14.5 (the IST), §7.7
//! (the 64-bit TSS), §11.5.4 (the APIC timer), §11.6.1 (the ICR), §11.9
//! (the spurious vector), §11.12 (x2APIC); vol. 2 (WRMSR, XSETBV, HLT);
//! vol. 4 (IA32_EFER, IA32_GS_BASE). No Linux source; no other kernel's
//! source.

use apic
use boot_info
use clock
use frames
use gdt
use log
use paging
use percpu
use timer

extern "c" fn pax_ap_halt()
extern "c" fn pax_rdmsr(msr: u64) -> u64
extern "c" fn pax_wrmsr(msr: u64, v: u64)
extern "c" fn pax_cr0() -> u64
extern "c" fn pax_cr2() -> u64
extern "c" fn pax_cr4() -> u64
extern "c" fn pax_set_cr0(v: u64)
extern "c" fn pax_set_cr4(v: u64)
extern "c" fn pax_xgetbv0() -> u64
extern "c" fn pax_xsetbv0(v: u64)
extern "c" fn pax_rdtsc() -> u64
extern "c" fn pax_pause()

extern "c" let pax_ap_hold: *u8
extern "c" let pax_ap_park: *u8
extern "c" let pax_ap_holds: *u8
extern "c" let pax_ist1_top: *u8
extern "c" let pax_ist2_top: *u8
extern "c" let pax_ist3_top: *u8
extern "c" let pax_ist4_top: *u8

/// Records PAX makes (CPU 0's included); a processor past them is left
/// parked in the bootloader's loop and counted.
pub const MAX: u64 = 64
/// The windows: PML4 slot 417, a processor's 256 KiB at CPUS + i × SPAN.
pub const CPUS: u64 = 0xffffd08000000000
pub const SPAN: u64 = 0x40000
const STACK_AT: u64 = 0x8000 // the idle stack's first byte
const IST_AT: u64 = 0x10000 // IST k's first byte: IST_AT + (k - 1) × IST_STEP
const IST_STEP: u64 = 0x8000
const STACK_BYTES: u64 = 0x4000
const PAGE: u64 = 4096
const WINDOW_KIB: u64 = 84 // 21 frames: the record and five stacks
/// An application processor's spurious-interrupt vector: 47 is gated
/// already (kernel/idt's 8259 line 15), and its low nibble is all ones, as
/// older processors require of the spurious vector (SDM vol. 3A §11.9).
pub const SPURIOUS_VECTOR: u64 = 47
/// CAUSE: the local APIC answered another APIC ID than Limine's.
const CAUSE_APIC: u64 = 0x1001

const EFER: u64 = 0xc0000080
const STAR: u64 = 0xc0000081
const LSTAR: u64 = 0xc0000082
const FMASK: u64 = 0xc0000084
const GS_BASE: u64 = 0xc0000101
const CR4_OSXSAVE: u64 = 0x40000

/// Limine's processors, the boot one included (1 without a response);
/// the windows made (indexes 1 to `made`); the bring-up's time.
var listed: u64 = 1
var made: u64 = 0
var took_ms: u64 = 0
var taken_kib: u64 = 0

/// Application processor `i`'s window (its record), i in 1..MAX.
pub fn window(i: u64) -> u64 {
    CPUS + i * SPAN
}

/// IST k's top in window `w` (k 1-4); k 0 the idle stack's.
fn top(w: u64, k: u64) -> u64 {
    if k == 0 {
        return w + STACK_AT + STACK_BYTES
    }
    w + IST_AT + (k - 1) * IST_STEP + STACK_BYTES
}

/// Limine's entry for index `i` (i ≥ 1): the i-th entry whose APIC ID is
/// not the boot processor's; the count past the end when there is none.
fn entry_of(i: u64) -> u64 {
    let n = boot_info.mp_count()
    let bsp = boot_info.mp_bsp()
    var seen: u64 = 0
    var j: u64 = 0
    while j < n {
        if boot_info.mp_apic(j) != bsp {
            seen += 1
            if seen == i {
                return j
            }
        }
        j += 1
    }
    n
}

/// `pages` zeroed frames mapped at `va` on, read-write, no-execute; false
/// when a frame or a table is refused (the window is left as it is: its
/// processor is never released).
fn back(pml4: u64, va: u64, pages: u64) -> bool {
    var k: u64 = 0
    while k < pages {
        let pa = frames.alloc() else 0
        if pa == 0 {
            return false
        }
        let v = pa + frames.hhdm()
        var i: u64 = 0
        while i < PAGE {
            // # Safety: the frame just taken, through the HHDM, 8-aligned.
            unsafe { ((v + i) as *u64).write_volatile(0) }
            i += 8
        }
        let m = paging.map(pml4, va + k * PAGE, pa, paging.RW | paging.NX) else 99
        if m == 99 {
            frames.free(pa)
            return false
        }
        k += 1
    }
    true
}

/// Application processor `i`'s window: its record, its GDT and TSS, its
/// five stacks. False when memory ran out.
fn make(pml4: u64, i: u64) -> bool {
    let w = window(i)
    if !back(pml4, w, 1) || !back(pml4, w + STACK_AT, STACK_BYTES / PAGE) {
        return false
    }
    var k: u64 = 1
    while k <= 4 {
        if !back(pml4, top(w, k) - STACK_BYTES, STACK_BYTES / PAGE) {
            return false
        }
        k += 1
    }
    let j = entry_of(i)
    percpu.put(w, percpu.ME, w)
    percpu.put(w, percpu.INDEX, i)
    percpu.put(w, percpu.CURRENT, percpu.IDLE_SLOT)
    percpu.put(w, percpu.APIC, boot_info.mp_apic(j))
    percpu.put(w, percpu.UID, boot_info.mp_uid(j))
    percpu.put(w, percpu.STACK, top(w, 0))
    percpu.put(w, percpu.KSTACK, top(w, 0))
    gdt.fill_ap(w, top(w, 0), top(w, 1), top(w, 2), top(w, 3), top(w, 4))
    true
}

/// Every application processor PAX does not run (`nosmp`, past MAX, a
/// window memory refused, or one that never reached its idle loop) is put
/// back where it was before the bootloader started it: INIT, and it waits
/// for a startup IPI (kernel/apic's `send_init`).
fn park(i: u64) {
    apic.send_init(apic_of(i))
}

/// Processor `i`'s two hold words in boot/isr.S's `pax_ap_holds` (i in
/// 1..MAX): 0 HELD, 1 its record.
fn holds(i: u64) -> u64 {
    // # Safety: the address of boot/isr.S's words; nothing is read.
    unsafe { pax_ap_holds as u64 } + i * 16
}

/// px161: first thing at the kernel's entry (kmain_console): every
/// application processor out of the bootloader's parked loop, which spins.
/// Each up to MAX goes to boot/isr.S's `pax_ap_hold` (`extra_argument` its
/// hold words), where it halts with interrupts off on the bootloader's
/// tables and stack until `start_aps`; under `nosmp`, and past MAX, to
/// `pax_ap_park`, halted for good until `start_aps` sends INIT. Nothing is
/// said: the log is not up yet.
pub fn hold() {
    let n = boot_info.mp_count()
    if n <= 1 {
        return
    }
    let none = boot_info.cmdline_has("nosmp")
    let bsp = boot_info.mp_bsp()
    var i: u64 = 1
    var j: u64 = 0
    while j < n {
        if boot_info.mp_apic(j) != bsp {
            let info = boot_info.mp_info(j)
            if i < MAX && !none {
                // # Safety: the processor's `struct limine_mp_info`
                // (Limine's, mapped in the HHDM): extra_argument (+24) is
                // the executable's to use; goto_address (+16) is stored
                // last, with release semantics, as PROTOCOL.md asks.
                unsafe {
                    ((info + 24) as *u64).write_volatile(holds(i))
                    ((info + 16) as *u64).atomic_store(pax_ap_hold as u64, Order.release)
                }
            } else {
                // # Safety: as above.
                unsafe { ((info + 16) as *u64).atomic_store(pax_ap_park as u64, Order.release) }
            }
            i += 1
        }
        j += 1
    }
}

/// px161: every application processor PAX runs given its window and let
/// on to its idle loop (kmain_console, after kernel/user's start: the boot
/// processor's CR0, CR4, EFER and SYSCALL MSRs are final then, and
/// kernel/timer has its calibration); the others sent INIT. `main` is
/// pax_ap_main's address (kmain_console names it: wolf names an export's
/// address only from another module).
pub fn start_aps(pml4: u64, main: u64) {
    let b = percpu.boot_record()
    percpu.put(b, percpu.APIC, apic.id())
    let n = boot_info.mp_count()
    if n == 0 {
        return
    }
    // # Safety: scalars the boot processor alone writes, interrupts off.
    unsafe { listed = n }
    var j: u64 = 0
    while j < n {
        if boot_info.mp_apic(j) == boot_info.mp_bsp() {
            percpu.put(b, percpu.UID, boot_info.mp_uid(j))
        }
        j += 1
    }
    if n == 1 {
        return
    }
    let aps = n - 1
    if boot_info.cmdline_has("nosmp") {
        var k: u64 = 1
        while k <= aps {
            park(k)
            k += 1
        }
        log.put("cpus: application processors left parked ")
        log.dec(aps as int)
        log.put(" of ")
        log.dec(aps as int)
        log.line(" (nosmp)")
        return
    }
    // The boot processor's control state, which each takes as its own.
    // # Safety: cpu.S's and fpu.S's reads of this processor's control
    // registers and MSRs; XGETBV only with CR4.OSXSAVE set.
    unsafe {
        let cr4 = pax_cr4()
        percpu.put_word(percpu.W_CR3, pml4)
        percpu.put_word(percpu.W_MAIN, main)
        percpu.put_word(percpu.W_CR0, pax_cr0())
        percpu.put_word(percpu.W_CR4, cr4)
        percpu.put_word(percpu.W_EFER, pax_rdmsr(EFER))
        percpu.put_word(percpu.W_XCR0, if cr4 & CR4_OSXSAVE != 0 { pax_xgetbv0() } else { 0 })
        percpu.put_word(percpu.W_STAR, pax_rdmsr(STAR))
        percpu.put_word(percpu.W_LSTAR, pax_rdmsr(LSTAR))
        percpu.put_word(percpu.W_FMASK, pax_rdmsr(FMASK))
        percpu.put_word(percpu.W_STOPPED, 0)
        percpu.put_word(percpu.W_REPORTED, 0)
    }
    let free0 = frames.free_count()
    var i: u64 = 1
    while i <= aps && i < MAX {
        if !make(pml4, i) {
            log.put("cpus: no memory for application processor ")
            log.dec(i as int)
            log.line("'s stacks; it and every later one left parked")
            i = MAX
        } else {
            // # Safety: as above.
            unsafe { made = i }
            i += 1
        }
    }
    let m = unsafe { made }
    i = m + 1
    while i <= aps {
        park(i) // past MAX, or no memory: back to waiting for a start
        i += 1
    }
    let t0 = clock.now_ns()
    i = 1
    while i <= m {
        let w = window(i)
        percpu.put(w, percpu.STATE, percpu.RELEASED)
        // # Safety: its second hold word (boot/isr.S's, 8-aligned): the
        // record stored with release semantics, so it and every word
        // published above are seen by the processor that reads it.
        unsafe { ((holds(i) + 8) as *u64).atomic_store(w, Order.release) }
        i += 1
    }
    // One NMI each, and only to a processor that says HELD: its gate is
    // loaded then, and it looks at its record only on that gate's return,
    // so the NMI is taken in the hold. One not held yet is asked again on
    // the next turn; one that never says so within the second gets no NMI
    // and is named below.
    var sent: u64 = 0 // by bit i (i < MAX, a word's bits)
    var waiting = true
    while waiting {
        i = 1
        while i <= m {
            let bit: u64 = 1 << i
            // # Safety: its first hold word, which the processor sets.
            if sent & bit == 0 && unsafe { (holds(i) as *u64).atomic_load(Order.acquire) } != 0 {
                apic.send_nmi(percpu.get(window(i), percpu.APIC))
                sent = sent | bit
            }
            i += 1
        }
        waiting = idle_count() < m && clock.now_ns() - t0 < 1000000000
        // # Safety: PAUSE; a polling loop's opaque call.
        unsafe { pax_pause() }
    }
    let ms = (clock.now_ns() - t0) / 1000000
    // # Safety: scalars the boot processor alone writes.
    unsafe {
        took_ms = ms
        taken_kib = (free0 - frames.free_count()) * 4
    }
    log.put("cpus: application processors idle ")
    log.dec(idle_count() as int)
    log.put(" of ")
    log.dec(aps as int)
    log.put(" in ")
    log.dec(ms as int)
    log.put(" ms, ")
    log.dec(WINDOW_KIB as int)
    log.put(" KiB each (")
    log.dec(unsafe { taken_kib } as int)
    log.line(" KiB with their tables); the boot processor runs every thread")
    if aps >= MAX {
        log.put("cpus: application processors past ")
        log.dec(MAX as int)
        log.put(" left parked: ")
        log.dec((aps - (MAX - 1)) as int)
        log.end()
    }
    i = 1
    while i <= m {
        if percpu.get(window(i), percpu.STATE) == percpu.RELEASED {
            log.put("cpus: cpu ")
            log.dec(i as int)
            log.put(" (apic ")
            log.dec(percpu.get(window(i), percpu.APIC) as int)
            log.line(") never reached its idle loop; put back to wait for a start")
            park(i)
        }
        i += 1
    }
    report_stops()
    check()
    if boot_info.cmdline_has("pax.cpunmi") {
        nmi_each()
    }
}

/// The processors whose record says IDLE now.
pub fn idle_count() -> u64 {
    var c: u64 = 0
    var i: u64 = 1
    while i <= unsafe { made } {
        if percpu.get(window(i), percpu.STATE) == percpu.IDLE {
            c += 1
        }
        i += 1
    }
    c
}

/// Processor `c`'s three tables and five stacks as checked: 0 its record
/// (GS's base as it read it), 1 its TSS, 2 its GDT, 3-7 its TSS's RSP0 and
/// IST1-4 (CPU 0's RSP0 follows its running thread, so 0 there).
fn item(c: u64, k: u64) -> u64 {
    let r = if c == 0 { percpu.boot_record() } else { window(c) }
    if k == 0 {
        return percpu.get(r, percpu.GS_SEEN)
    }
    if k == 1 {
        return percpu.get(r, percpu.TSS)
    }
    if k == 2 {
        return percpu.get(r, percpu.GDT)
    }
    if c == 0 && k == 3 {
        return 0
    }
    gdt.tss_stack(percpu.get(r, percpu.TSS), k - 3)
}

fn item_name(k: u64) -> str {
    if k == 0 { return "record (GS)" }
    if k == 1 { return "TSS" }
    if k == 2 { return "GDT" }
    if k == 3 { return "RSP0 stack" }
    if k == 4 { return "IST1 stack" }
    if k == 5 { return "IST2 stack" }
    if k == 6 { return "IST3 stack" }
    "IST4 stack"
}

/// Where processor `c`'s item `k` must be: CPU 0's boot/isr.S storage, an
/// application processor's own window.
fn expected(c: u64, k: u64) -> u64 {
    if c == 0 {
        // # Safety: link-time addresses; nothing is read.
        unsafe {
            if k == 0 { return percpu.boot_record() }
            if k == 4 { return pax_ist1_top as u64 }
            if k == 5 { return pax_ist2_top as u64 }
            if k == 6 { return pax_ist3_top as u64 }
            if k == 7 { return pax_ist4_top as u64 }
        }
        return item(c, k)
    }
    let w = window(c)
    if k == 0 { return w }
    if k == 1 { return w + percpu.TSS_AREA }
    if k == 2 { return w + percpu.GDT_AREA }
    top(w, k - 3)
}

/// The private-state check, over every window `release` made, whatever its
/// processor reached (and CPU 0): its record, TSS, GDT and stacks where its
/// own must be, and no two alike. GS's base as the processor read it counts
/// only once it entered PAX (it writes GS_SEEN first).
fn check() {
    let m = unsafe { made }
    var bad: u64 = 0
    var c: u64 = 0
    while c <= m {
        var k: u64 = 0
        while k < 8 {
            let counts = k != 0 || c == 0 || percpu.get(window(c), percpu.STATE) != percpu.RELEASED
            let v = item(c, k)
            if counts && v != expected(c, k) {
                log.put("cpus: private state: cpu ")
                log.dec(c as int)
                log.put("'s ")
                log.put(item_name(k))
                log.put(" is ")
                log.hex(v)
                log.put(", not its own ")
                log.hex(expected(c, k))
                log.end()
                bad += 1
            }
            var d: u64 = 0
            while d < c {
                if counts && v != 0 && v == item(d, k) {
                    log.put("cpus: private state: cpu ")
                    log.dec(c as int)
                    log.put(" and cpu ")
                    log.dec(d as int)
                    log.put(" share a ")
                    log.put(item_name(k))
                    log.put(", ")
                    log.hex(v)
                    log.end()
                    bad += 1
                }
                d += 1
            }
            k += 1
        }
        c += 1
    }
    if bad == 0 {
        log.put("cpus: private state checked: ")
        log.dec((m + 1) as int)
        log.line(" processors, no record, GDT, TSS or stack shared")
    }
}

/// `pax.cpunmi` (a test's word): one NMI to each idle processor by its
/// local APIC (kernel/apic's `send_nmi`), then a second by kernel/clock for
/// each to count it; each must have taken it on its own IST2.
fn nmi_each() {
    let m = unsafe { made }
    var want: u64 = 0
    var i: u64 = 1
    while i <= m {
        let w = window(i)
        if percpu.get(w, percpu.STATE) == percpu.IDLE {
            want += 1
            apic.send_nmi(percpu.get(w, percpu.APIC))
        }
        i += 1
    }
    let t0 = clock.now_ns()
    var took: u64 = 0
    var own: u64 = 0
    var waiting = true
    while waiting {
        took = 0
        own = 0
        i = 1
        while i <= m {
            let w = window(i)
            if percpu.get(w, percpu.STATE) == percpu.IDLE && percpu.get(w, percpu.NMIS) != 0 {
                took += 1
                let at = percpu.get(w, percpu.NMI_AT)
                if at >= top(w, 2) - STACK_BYTES && at < top(w, 2) {
                    own += 1
                }
            }
            i += 1
        }
        waiting = took < want && clock.now_ns() - t0 < 1000000000
        // # Safety: PAUSE.
        unsafe { pax_pause() }
    }
    log.put("cpus: application processors took an NMI each ")
    log.dec(took as int)
    log.put(" of ")
    log.dec(want as int)
    if own == took {
        log.line(", each on its own stack")
    } else {
        log.put("; on its own stack ")
        log.dec(own as int)
        log.end()
    }
}

/// px161: where Limine's parked processor goes (boot/isr.S's pax_ap_entry
/// jumps here with its record, on its own stack, its GDT, TSS, IDT and GS
/// loaded). Never returns.
export fn pax_ap_main(rec: u64) {
    // # Safety: isr.S's RDMSR of IA32_GS_BASE, which pax_ap_entry set.
    percpu.put(rec, percpu.GS_SEEN, unsafe { pax_rdmsr(GS_BASE) })
    // # Safety: the boot processor's control state (`start_aps` published
    // it before the record): the same CPU model's bits, CR4.OSXSAVE before
    // XSETBV; EFER's LME and LMA as they already are.
    unsafe {
        pax_set_cr0(percpu.word(percpu.W_CR0))
        let cr4 = percpu.word(percpu.W_CR4)
        pax_set_cr4(cr4)
        if cr4 & CR4_OSXSAVE != 0 {
            pax_xsetbv0(percpu.word(percpu.W_XCR0))
        }
        pax_wrmsr(EFER, percpu.word(percpu.W_EFER))
        pax_wrmsr(STAR, percpu.word(percpu.W_STAR))
        pax_wrmsr(LSTAR, percpu.word(percpu.W_LSTAR))
        pax_wrmsr(FMASK, percpu.word(percpu.W_FMASK))
    }
    let id = apic.ap_start(SPURIOUS_VECTOR)
    if id != percpu.get(rec, percpu.APIC) {
        percpu.stop(CAUSE_APIC, id, 0, 0)
    }
    timer.ap_arm()
    // # Safety: fpu.S's RDTSC.
    percpu.put(rec, percpu.TSC, unsafe { pax_rdtsc() })
    percpu.put(rec, percpu.STATE, percpu.IDLE)
    while true {
        percpu.count(percpu.WAKES)
        // # Safety: isr.S's STI; HLT; CLI: the processor sleeps until its
        // next interrupt, every one of which has a gate.
        unsafe { pax_ap_halt() }
    }
}

/// Word `i` of boot/isr.S's frame at `f`.
fn frame(f: u64, i: u64) -> u64 {
    // # Safety: the trampoline's frame (22 words), live for this handler.
    unsafe { ((f + i * 8) as *u64).read_volatile() }
}

/// An application processor's interrupt (kernel/interrupts, every vector
/// but the NMI): its tick, its spurious vector, or a stop. The frame to
/// resume: `f` itself.
pub fn ap_interrupt(f: u64) -> u64 {
    let v = frame(f, 15)
    if v == timer.MASTER_BASE {
        percpu.count(percpu.TICKS)
        apic.eoi()
        return f
    }
    if v == SPURIOUS_VECTOR {
        percpu.count(percpu.SPURIOUS)
        return f
    }
    // # Safety: cpu.S's MOV from CR2 (the page fault's address for 14).
    let cr2 = if v == 14 { unsafe { pax_cr2() } } else { 0 }
    percpu.stop(v, frame(f, 16), frame(f, 17), cr2)
}

/// An application processor's NMI (on its own IST2): counted, the frame's
/// address kept, and it resumes.
pub fn ap_nmi(f: u64) {
    percpu.count(percpu.NMIS)
    percpu.put(percpu.mine(), percpu.NMI_AT, f)
}

/// CPU 0, at each tick and after the bring-up: each processor that has
/// stopped since the last call, named once.
pub fn report_stops() {
    let s = percpu.stopped()
    let r = percpu.word(percpu.W_REPORTED)
    if s == r {
        return
    }
    var i: u64 = 1
    while i < MAX {
        let bit: u64 = 1 << i
        if s & bit != 0 && r & bit == 0 {
            let w = window(i)
            let cause = percpu.get(w, percpu.CAUSE)
            log.put("cpus: cpu ")
            log.dec(i as int)
            log.put(" stopped: ")
            if cause == percpu.CAUSE_SCHED {
                log.put("entered the scheduler, rip ")
                log.hex(percpu.get(w, percpu.RIP))
            } else if cause == CAUSE_APIC {
                log.put("its local APIC answered APIC ID ")
                log.dec(percpu.get(w, percpu.ERROR) as int)
                log.put(", the bootloader's ")
                log.dec(percpu.get(w, percpu.APIC) as int)
            } else {
                log.put("vector ")
                log.dec(cause as int)
                log.put(" error ")
                log.hex(percpu.get(w, percpu.ERROR))
                log.put(" rip ")
                log.hex(percpu.get(w, percpu.RIP))
                log.put(" cr2 ")
                log.hex(percpu.get(w, percpu.CR2))
            }
            log.end()
        }
        i += 1
    }
    percpu.put_word(percpu.W_REPORTED, s)
}

// --- /proc/pax-cpus's lines (kernel/procfs) -----------------------------------

/// The processors the bootloader listed, the boot one included (1 with no
/// MP response).
pub fn total() -> u64 {
    // # Safety: a scalar written once by `start_aps`.
    unsafe { listed }
}

/// Processors that entered PAX: CPU 0 and each released one that reached
/// its idle loop (stopped since or not).
pub fn started() -> u64 {
    var c: u64 = 1
    var i: u64 = 1
    while i <= unsafe { made } {
        let s = percpu.get(window(i), percpu.STATE)
        if s == percpu.IDLE || s == percpu.STOPPED {
            c += 1
        }
        i += 1
    }
    c
}

/// Processor `i`'s record, 0 when it has none (parked: `nosmp`, past MAX,
/// or out of memory).
pub fn record(i: u64) -> u64 {
    if i == 0 {
        return percpu.boot_record()
    }
    if i > unsafe { made } {
        return 0
    }
    window(i)
}

/// Processor `i`'s APIC ID, from its record or, parked, Limine's entry.
pub fn apic_of(i: u64) -> u64 {
    let r = record(i)
    if r != 0 {
        return percpu.get(r, percpu.APIC)
    }
    boot_info.mp_apic(entry_of(i))
}

/// CPU 0's tick count: kernel/timer's (its ticks are the boot processor's
/// timer's, counted there).
pub fn boot_ticks() -> u64 {
    timer.delivered()
}

/// The bring-up's time, in ms (0 before or without one).
pub fn took() -> u64 {
    // # Safety: a scalar written once by `start_aps`.
    unsafe { took_ms }
}
